@startuml
title auth UI visual states

[*] --> EmptyForm
EmptyForm --> Submitting : user clicks Sign In
Submitting --> Success : valid credentials
Submitting --> AuthenticationFailed : 401 generic failure

AuthenticationFailed --> EmptyForm : user edits input
Success --> MeLoading : protected route loads
MeLoading --> AuthenticatedHome : /me returns 200
MeLoading --> SessionRejected : /me returns 401
SessionRejected --> EmptyForm : token cleared and redirected
AuthenticatedHome --> ChangePasswordSubmitting : user submits change password
ChangePasswordSubmitting --> AuthenticatedHome : success
ChangePasswordSubmitting --> ChangePasswordFailed : generic password-action error
ChangePasswordFailed --> AuthenticatedHome : user retries or dismisses
AuthenticatedHome --> ForgotPasswordSubmitting : forgot/reset flow in local PoC
ForgotPasswordSubmitting --> ForgotPasswordIssued : reset token returned
ForgotPasswordIssued --> ResetPasswordSubmitting : user submits reset token
ResetPasswordSubmitting --> ResetPasswordSuccess : valid token
ResetPasswordSubmitting --> ResetPasswordFailed : invalid token or bad request

state EmptyForm
state Submitting
state Success
state AuthenticationFailed
state MeLoading
state SessionRejected
state AuthenticatedHome
state ChangePasswordSubmitting
state ChangePasswordFailed
state ForgotPasswordSubmitting
state ForgotPasswordIssued
state ResetPasswordSubmitting
state ResetPasswordSuccess
state ResetPasswordFailed

note right of AuthenticationFailed
Visual test should confirm
generic auth failure copy and styling.
No account-state-specific leakage
should be visible in the UI.
end note

note right of Success
Successful login state should
store a JWT returned from the
current auth boundary, but the
authenticated UI should wait for
`GET /me` to confirm the session.
end note

note right of ForgotPasswordIssued
The current PoC exposes the reset
token in the response so the flow
is usable without an email/SMS
delivery integration.
end note

@enduml
